From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: empty ISR must not ACK bits it did not read

0017 dispatches when INT_ST==0 and INT_RAW has ESP_SLAVE_RX_NEW_PACKET_INT
(BIT 23). The else path still wrote ESP_SLAVE_INT_CLR_KNOWN, which
includes BIT 23. Cold 4-way after msg2 shows empty raw=0x004cf800: BIT 23
is not latched yet, unnamed bits hold DAT1, and the superset clear can
ACK a msg3 that arrives between the RAW read and INT_CLR write. That
packet is never delivered. 0017 successful captures had BIT 23 already
set in RAW (0x00ccf800), so they never entered this else.

Keep 0017: RAW BIT 23 promotes and acknowledges only that bit.
Keep 0011: a true all-zero RAW still uses CLR_KNOWN so the boot DAT1
spin stays dead. When RAW is nonzero without BIT 23, write that RAW
value. Do not fabricate RX from those bits. Do not clear BIT 23 unless
this read observed it.

What this cannot see: if the AP never sends msg3, RAW BIT 23 will not
set. If unnamed bits are not write-1-to-clear, DAT1 can still stick;
that is a remaining slave-side question, not a licence to ACK unseen
RX. The negative tests are: boot has no 254x status=0x00000000 storm;
cold 4-way has msg3 00 97 and two 08 02; after msg2, empty
raw=0x004cf800 is followed by empty-raw-ack of that value, not by a
dropped packet and Command[0x6] timeout.

---
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -232,6 +232,8 @@
 	struct esp_sdio_context *context = NULL;
 	u32 *int_status;
 	u32 status_read;
+	u32 raw;
+	int raw_ret;
 	bool dispatch;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -273,10 +275,11 @@
 	CHECK_SDIO_RW_ERROR(ret);
 
 	status_read = ret ? 0 : *int_status;
+	raw = 0;
+	raw_ret = 0;
 
 	if (!status_read) {
-		u32 raw = 0;
-		int raw_ret = esp_read_reg(context, ESP_SLAVE_INT_RAW_REG,
+		raw_ret = esp_read_reg(context, ESP_SLAVE_INT_RAW_REG,
 				(u8 *) &raw, sizeof(raw), ACQUIRE_LOCK);
 
 		/*
@@ -309,7 +312,19 @@
 		*int_status = status_read;
 	} else {
 		empty_isr_streak++;
-		*int_status = ESP_SLAVE_INT_CLR_KNOWN;
+		/*
+		 * CLR_KNOWN includes BIT 23.  Writing it here after a RAW
+		 * sample that did not contain BIT 23 can acknowledge msg3
+		 * unseen.  Ack only the bits this read observed.  RAW==0
+		 * still uses CLR_KNOWN for the boot DAT1 spin.
+		 */
+		if (!raw_ret && raw) {
+			esp_info("SDIO IRQ empty-raw-ack: streak=%u raw=0x%08x\n",
+				 empty_isr_streak, raw);
+			*int_status = raw;
+		} else {
+			*int_status = ESP_SLAVE_INT_CLR_KNOWN;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Clear interrupt status */
